{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"r1","type":"claim","text":"In a flat of three co-equal members nobody holds authority over the others; any chore arrangement one member designs, convenes and records will be experienced by the other two as management. On this reading, later reinterpretation of agreements and avoidance of the conversations are not two independent defects but the two available responses of equals to being managed.","scope":"co-equal flatmates sharing a household","grounds":"the asker is one of three equals; the input account's remedies (unilateral posted confirmations, a weekly look someone convenes) are asker-initiated and asker-run","bearing":"shifts the design goal from clarity alone to legitimacy: who owns the design, not how well it is written"},{"id":"r2","type":"claim","text":"Most 'what did the agreement mean' disputes attach to the seams between two people's contributions — I did the counters, you said you'd do the floor. Assigning a whole space to a single owner removes the seams and with them much of the dispute's object.","bearing":"motivates r3"},{"id":"r3","type":"commitment","text":"Allocate each common area as an owned domain: one owner, responsible end to end, answerable to a written floor and free to exceed it as they please.","action":"collect private, asynchronous rankings (message each person the list of areas, ask which they mind most and least) and match owners to tolerances rather than holding a live negotiation the avoidant friend can simply not attend; set the floor at a level all three can genuinely accept, not at the cleanest member's preference","consequence":"allocation reflects real tolerances; inside a single owner's domain there is nothing whose meaning two people can disagree about","depends":["r1","r2"]},{"id":"r4","type":"commitment","text":"Put the specification where the work happens rather than where the talk happens: a checklist inside the cupboard door, taped to the bin lid, on the bathroom mirror, plus one gap-filler rule agreed once — where nothing is written at the spot, the default standard is X.","consequence":"the standard is consultable by whoever is doing the task at the moment they do it, survives schedule changes, and does not require anyone to convene or attend a conversation","revises":["ad92700706f3372d"]},{"id":"r5","type":"objection","text":"The input account's standing unilateral confirmations (I've got X, you've got Y), useful as one-off corrections, consolidate the asker's clerk-of-record role when run as a habit; the device that fixes ambiguity can deepen the legitimacy problem that may be driving the withdrawal.","target":["ad92700706f3372d"],"bearing":"this objection is itself criticisable: if the friend's withdrawal has an unrelated cause, the clerk-role reading is wrong and the device is harmless; if the account's own caution about visible apparatus applies to its own records, the objection gains force"},{"id":"r6","type":"commitment","text":"Rotate the chair: the member who convenes, records and adjusts the arrangements serves a week or a month at a time, so each of the three is sometime designer and sometime subject.","action":"hand the avoidant friend the chair on the same terms as everyone else rather than interviewing them about it first","consequence":"the arrangement reads as ours rather than the asker's, and the withdrawal is offered a structural route back in","depends":["r1"]},{"id":"r7","type":"use","text":"Take up the input account's one-on-one, non-accusing conversation with the avoidant friend, but change the question from difficulty to stakes: not what makes these conversations hard, but whether they want the flat at this standard at all or whether it is the other two's project being run on them.","target":["ad92700706f3372d"],"depends":["r1"],"consequence":"a stakes answer calls for a trade (r8); a difficulty answer calls for changes to the talk's format and character"},{"id":"r8","type":"commitment","text":"Where tolerances genuinely differ, trade across domains rather than enforce uniform standards: a lower common floor; or cleaning load swapped against the admin nobody wants (bills, shopping, landlord calls); or a small rent adjustment.","consequence":"a low-stakes member stops being an enforcement target, which is one plausible reading of the withdrawal — though only a reading; the material does not say why the friend avoids the talks","depends":["r1"],"mentions":["ad92700706f3372d"]},{"id":"r9","type":"claim","text":"The rotation in r6 doubles as a diagnostic: if the friend re-engages while holding the chair, the withdrawal tracked the management structure; if they withdraw even while holding it, the cause probably is not the chores at all and the one-on-one conversation becomes the necessary move.","depends":["r6"],"bearing":"the test is imperfect — chairing may be aversive in itself — but it discriminates between conjectures the material leaves unsettled"},{"id":"r10","type":"use","text":"Take up the input account's structural exits (a cleaner split three ways, shrinking the shared surface, renegotiating whether the living arrangement is working) as legitimate endpoints rather than failures, together with its caution against over-engineering; both stay live if the trades in r8 fail.","target":["ad92700706f3372d"]},{"id":"r11","type":"problem","text":"This design trades flexibility for clarity: whole-domain ownership is more brittle under shifting schedules than the input account's weekly swap planning. Deputy defaults (a named fallback per area when the owner is away) and monthly rather than weekly adjustment are partial answers, not a resolution.","mentions":["ad92700706f3372d"]},{"id":"r12","type":"problem","text":"Private preference rankings can be gamed: someone may overstate how much they mind an area to capture an easy domain. Periodic rotation of the least-preferred domain, or allowing paid substitution, are candidate mitigations; neither is tested here.","depends":["r3"]},{"id":"r13","type":"problem","text":"The input account's commitment surface is not supplied in this exchange, so uptake can address only its exposed body (ad92700706f3372d); its records, if any, cannot be used or objected to from here."}],"uptake":["r3","r4","r6","r7","r8","r9","r10"]}